response:
 Since $|x + y - 7| \geq 0$ and $|4x - y + 12| \geq 0$, the left side of the equation can only be zero if both absolute value terms are zero. Otherwise, the whole equation is greater than 0. Therefore, we have the following system of linear equations: \[
\begin{cases}
x + y - 7 = 0 \\
4x - y + 12 = 0
\end{cases}
\] By adding the two equations, we get $5x + 5 = 0$, so $x = -1$. Substituting $x = -1$ into the first equation, we get $-1 + y - 7 = 0$, so $y = 8$. Thus, the ordered pair is $(-1, 8)$. </think> <answer> $(-1, 8)$ </answer>

